<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-5697] Web Console should be configurable for IPv4 connections</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-5697</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When an IPv6 network interface is available, NodeJS will always prefer that to an IPv4 interface.  This causes problems if IPv6 is not fully operational on the network.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This fix will add the ability to specify that IPv4 should be used.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13084700">IGNITE-5697</key>
            <summary>Web Console should be configurable for IPv4 connections</summary>
                <type id="1" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/viewavatar?size=xsmall&amp;avatarId=21133&amp;avatarType=issuetype">Bug</type>
                                            <priority id="3" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/priorities/major.svg">Major</priority>
                        <status id="6" iconUrl="https://issues.apache.org/jira/images/icons/statuses/closed.png" description="The issue is considered finished, the resolution is correct. Issues which are not closed can be reopened.">Closed</status>
                    <statusCategory id="3" key="done" colorName="green"/>
                                    <resolution id="1">Fixed</resolution>
                                        <assignee username="anovikov">Andrey Novikov</assignee>
                                    <reporter username="endian675">Michael Griggs</reporter>
                        <labels>
                    </labels>
                <created>Wed, 5 Jul 2017 07:35:49 +0000</created>
                <updated>Fri, 12 Jan 2018 02:15:45 +0000</updated>
                            <resolved>Fri, 12 Jan 2018 02:15:37 +0000</resolved>
                                    <version>2.0</version>
                                    <fixVersion>2.3</fixVersion>
                                    <component>wizards</component>
                        <due></due>
                            <votes>0</votes>
                                    <watches>3</watches>
                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="16074358" author="michael.griggs@gridgain.com" created="Wed, 5 Jul 2017 07:39:27 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;For the implementation we can either&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;1.  Make an IPv4/IPv6 flag in configuration.&lt;br/&gt;
or&lt;br/&gt;
2.  Allow the host parameter to be configured, so that the server can be bound to any specific IP address on the machine.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16074366" author="michael.griggs@gridgain.com" created="Wed, 5 Jul 2017 07:43:03 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;There appears to be a bug in NodeJS such that when [1] is called, a Server object is returned by when [2] is called a null value is returned.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Therefore a workaround will be necessary when passing the server object to the &quot;onListening&quot; function.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;[1]: &lt;tt&gt;server.listen(3000);&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;[2]: &lt;tt&gt;server.listen(3000,&apos;0.0.0.0&apos;);&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
</comment>
                            <comment id="16074920" author="anovikov" created="Wed, 5 Jul 2017 15:15:28 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;According this &lt;a href=&quot;https://nodejs.org/api/net.html#net_server_listen_port_host_backlog_callback&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;documentation&lt;/a&gt; &amp;lt;net.Server&amp;gt; should be returned when &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;2&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=michael.griggs%40gridgain.com&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;michael.griggs@gridgain.com&quot;&gt;michael.griggs@gridgain.com&lt;/a&gt;, on which NodeJS version you see such behavior?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16074927" author="michael.griggs@gridgain.com" created="Wed, 5 Jul 2017 15:19:32 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=anovikov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;anovikov&quot;&gt;anovikov&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;mgriggs@ubuntu-16:~$ nodejs -v&lt;br/&gt;
v6.11.0&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16323432" author="anovikov" created="Fri, 12 Jan 2018 02:14:47 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This problem was fixed by adding host parameter in settings: &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;srv.listen(settings.server.port, settings.server.host)&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By default settings.server.host = &apos;127.0.0.1&apos;, settings.server.port = 3000&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
